## Module 2 — Stage & Earnings Analysis

### Stage Classification (Weinstein)
From each stock's candle data extract:
`ma50`, `ma150`, `ma200`, `slope200`, `high_1y`, `low_1y`, `pct_from_high`

| Stage | Condition |
|---|---|
| **Stage 2** ✅ | price > ma50 > ma150 > ma200, slope200 > 0 |
| **Stage 1** 🔵 | price ≈ ma200 (±5%), slope200 ≈ 0 |
| **Stage 3** ⚠️ | price choppy around ma200, slope200 flattening |
| **Stage 4** 🔴 | price < ma50 < ma150 < ma200, slope200 < 0 |

### Earnings + Concall (parallel WebSearches)
One query per stock, fired simultaneously:
```
WebSearch("<STOCK_NAME> quarterly results concall Q4 FY26 OR Q3 FY26 management guidance site:screener.in OR site:trendlyne.com OR site:moneycontrol.com OR site:businessstandard.com")
```

**Trusted sources only:** `screener.in`, `trendlyne.com`, `tickertape.in`,
`moneycontrol.com`, `economictimes.indiatimes.com`, `businessstandard.com`,
`livemint.com`, `bseindia.com`, `nseindia.com`

Per stock, produce:
1. Company overview (8–10 pts: business, segments, moat, promoters, geography)
2. One-line summary
3. Guidance & Outlook (8–10 pts with specific numbers)
4. Strategic Updates (8–10 pts)
5. Earnings Triggers (8–10 pts)
6. Risks (8–10 pts, management's own words)
7. Key Q&A (8–10 exchanges)
8. Management Consistency (8–10 points + ⭐ credibility score 1–5)
9. Investor Verdict (3–5 sentences)

### Action per stock
| Action | When |
|---|---|
| TRACKING | weight ≤ 0.2% |
| ✅ STRONG HOLD | Stage 2B, earnings accelerating |
| HOLD | Stage 2, earnings steady |
| WATCH | Stage 1 or mixed signals |
| TRIM | Stage 3, earnings slowing, or weight >15% |
| EXIT | Stage 4, thesis broken (NOT triggered by small size) |
| ADD | Stage 2A fresh breakout + earnings confirmation |

