## HTML Report Output

Write a 4-tab dark-mode HTML report to `~/Desktop/portfolio-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html`.
Write in **4 sequential Bash `cat >>` appends** (never one giant string).

### Part 1 (`cat >`)
Head + styles + Tab 1 (Overview: snapshot banner + stat grid + holdings table + allocation)

### Part 2 (`cat >>`)
Tab 2 (Performance: benchmark table + visual bars + stock returns + insights)

### Part 3 (`cat >>`)
Tab 3 (Stage Analysis: summary table + sidebar stock selector + all stock detail cards)

### Part 4 (`cat >>`)
Tab 4 (Rebalancing: priority list + reallocation table + health scores) + `</body></html>` + JS

### UI Standards (never deviate)
```
--bg: #0f1117  --surface: #1a1d27  --surface2: #22263a  --border: #2e3250
--text: #e2e8f0  --muted: #8892b0  --green: #22c55e  --red: #ef4444
--yellow: #f59e0b  --blue: #60a5fa  --purple: #a78bfa  --accent: #6366f1
```

Stage badges: `.stage-2 { background:#14532d; color:#4ade80; border:1px solid #16a34a }`
Action badges: `.action-hold { background:#1e3a5f; color:#93c5fd }`

Tab navigation uses `showTab(name, btn)` — pass `this` explicitly, never use `event.target`.
Stock detail panel uses `showStock(symbol)` with sidebar on desktop, dropdown on mobile.

After writing: `open ~/Desktop/portfolio-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html`

